---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/astro/Breadcrumb.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Cookie and Technology Notice | Gibraltar For Sale" description="Cookie and similar technology notice for the current Gibraltar For Sale information website.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px] px-5 pb-20 pt-10 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-sea-700">Cookie and technology notice</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink-900 sm:text-6xl">Cookies and similar technologies</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-stone-600">Last reviewed 10 November 2026</p>
    <div class="article-content mt-8">
      <p>The current site has no first-party login, contact form, waitlist or saved-search feature, so it does not need those features' application cookies. Its source does not intentionally add Google Analytics, advertising pixels or session-replay tools.</p>
      <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and analytics settings</h2>
      <p>The site is served by Netlify. Hosting may use technical identifiers or process request data for service delivery and security. Whether optional Netlify Analytics is enabled is controlled in the hosting account and cannot be established from the public source repository. The site operator must verify the dashboard setting and update this notice before claiming either that analytics is active or that no analytics is used.</p>
      <h2 id="external">External links</h2>
      <p>Links to other websites—including official sources, Wikimedia Commons and Unsplash—take you outside this site. Those providers set and describe their own technologies.</p>
      <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can manage or clear cookies through your browser. This notice does not imply that a browser choice controls server-side security logs. If optional analytics, advertising or other non-essential storage is enabled later, the operator should review applicable consent requirements and provide suitable controls before activation.</p>
      <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
      <p>Verified operator contact details are not yet published. See the <a href="/privacy/" class="font-bold text-sea-700 underline">Privacy notice</a> for the current status.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
